        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "Defendant and an acquaintance agreed to break into an unoccupied dwelling house at night to steal firearms[cite: 53]. When they reached the house, the acquaintance broke a basement window with a rock, and both men climbed inside[cite: 53]. While searching the living room, the acquaintance used an iron pry bar to force open a locked gun cabinet[cite: 53]. An armed neighbor who lived nearby heard breaking glass, walked over with a rifle, and observed the two men inside through an open window[cite: 53]. The neighbor pointed the rifle through the window and shouted, 'Freeze, police!'[cite: 53] The acquaintance turned toward the window and raised the iron pry bar in a threatening manner[cite: 53]. Believing the acquaintance was about to attack, the neighbor fired a shot in lawful self-defense, striking the acquaintance in the chest and killing him instantly[cite: 53]. Defendant immediately dropped to the floor and surrendered[cite: 53]. The jurisdiction follows the common law 'agency theory' of felony murder[cite: 53].",
